>>
Rule 1 (tensor must have at least one dimension)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 2 (tensor must be compatible with index tuple in size)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 4 (indexing dimension should be within bounds)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : v_2[i] < shape(v_1, 0)
>>
Rule 5 (tensor must not have zero-sized dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 6 (value tensor should match destination tensor size)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 7 (tensor must have compatible dimensions for indexing)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) ≠ 0
